RayCAD patch to OCCT 8.0.1 (LGPL-2.1 with the OCCT exception; this file is under the same terms).

What: BRepMesh_ModelHealer heals the faces of the model one after another, also when IMeshTools_Parameters::InParallel
is set: its face loop in performInternal() and the second face loop in amplifyEdges() run single-threaded. Edge
discretisation, the edge amplification step and face meshing stay parallel.

Why: with InParallel, ThreadSanitizer (OCCT built with -fsanitize=thread) reports a data race inside one
BRepMesh_IncrementalMesh call made from a single thread: BRepMesh_ModelHealer::fixFaceBoundaries ->
connectClosestPoints -> adjustSamePoints writes pcurve end points (BRepMesh_ModelHealer.hxx adjustSamePoints,
*theMajorSamePnt1 = *theMinorSamePnt1) on one pool thread while BRepMesh_FaceChecker::perform ->
BndBox2dTreeSelector::Accept -> BRepMesh_GeomTool::IntSegSeg reads the same 2D points on another thread, both inside
the parallel face loop of BRepMesh_ModelHealer::performInternal. Seen on RayCAD's corpus part
raycad-synthetic/circular_pocket_1.stp at 0.02 mm / 0.2 rad (tests/unit/kernel/mesh_test.cpp "[.meshcorpus]"), and 15
distinct such reports over the naming tests' 20 corpus parts. Unsynchronised writes and reads of the same doubles are
undefined behaviour, and the healer's result decides which faces are re-meshed, so the mesh can depend on timing.
Healing is a small part of a mesh call (wires are checked once per face); running it serially removes the race and
leaves the meshes unchanged (they are bit-identical to single-threaded meshing in RayCAD's tests either way).

Upstream: not reported. The face loop of BRepMesh_ModelHealer::performInternal is parallel in OCCT master as of
2026-11-20.

diff --git a/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKMesh/BRepMesh/BRepMesh_ModelHealer.cxx b/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKMesh/BRepMesh/BRepMesh_ModelHealer.cxx
--- a/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKMesh/BRepMesh/BRepMesh_ModelHealer.cxx
+++ b/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKMesh/BRepMesh/BRepMesh_ModelHealer.cxx
@@ -149,7 +149,9 @@
   }

   // TODO: Here we can process edges in order to remove close discrete points.
-  OSD_Parallel::For(0, myModel->FacesNb(), *this, !isParallel());
+  // RayCAD: faces are healed one at a time; in parallel, fixFaceBoundaries on one face raced with the
+  // FaceChecker of another on the same pcurve points (ThreadSanitizer).
+  OSD_Parallel::For(0, myModel->FacesNb(), *this, true);
   amplifyEdges();

   IMeshData::DMapOfIFacePtrsMapOfIEdgePtrs::Iterator aFaceIt(*myFaceIntersectingEdges);
@@ -203,7 +205,7 @@
     OSD_Parallel::ForEach(aFacesToCheck.cbegin(),
                           aFacesToCheck.cend(),
                           *this,
-                          !myParameters.InParallel || aFacesToCheck.Length() <= 1,
+                          true, // RayCAD: see performInternal
                           aFacesToCheck.Length());

     aEdgesToUpdate.Clear();
